oke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 2L3 6v14a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2V6l-3-4z\"></path><line x1=\"3\" y1=\"6\" x2=\"21\" y2=\"6\"></line><path d=\"M16 10a4 4 0 01-8 0\"></path></svg></button><button class=\"flex lg:hidden h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-button text-foreground-muted transition-colors duration-150 hover:bg-surface-hover cursor-pointer\" aria-label=\"Toggle menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\"><svg width=\"18\" height=\"18\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"7\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"7\"></line><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"12\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"12\"></line><line x1=\"4\" y1=\"17\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"17\"></line></svg></button></div></div></header><div class=\"w-full border-b border-border/40 bg-surface-elevated/80 dark:bg-surface-elevated/40 backdrop-blur-sm relative z-40\" id=\"global-search-bar\"><div class=\"relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6\"><div class=\"flex items-center h-11 gap-3\"><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"text-brand-500/60 dark:text-brand-400/50 shrink-0\"><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"11\" r=\"8\"></circle><line x1=\"21\" y1=\"21\" x2=\"16.65\" y2=\"16.65\"></line></svg><input type=\"text\" placeholder=\"Search products, certificates, articles, or batch numbers...\" class=\"flex-1 bg-transparent text-[13px] text-foreground placeholder:text-foreground-muted/50 outline-none tracking-wide\" autocomplete=\"off\" value=\"\"></div></div></div><main class=\"no-overflow-x flex-1\"><div class=\"page-enter\"><section class=\"pt-6 sm:pt-8 pb-16 text-readable\"><div class=\"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[11px] font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 accent-glow mb-3\">Montreal<!-- -->, <!-- -->QC</p><h1 class=\"text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-foreground\">Research Peptides in Montreal</h1><div class=\"mt-4 w-12 h-px bg-brand-300/50 dark:bg-border-strong\"></div><dl class=\"mt-6 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-3 sm:grid-cols-3\"><div><dt class=\"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Ships from</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-[14px] text-foreground\">Within Canada</dd></div><div><dt class=\"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Typical transit</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-[14px] text-foreground\">2 business days</dd></div><div><dt class=\"font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Customs</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-[14px] text-foreground\">None — domestic</dd></div></dl><div class=\"mt-7 space-y-4\"><p class=\"text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Montreal runs to about two business days on Canada Post Xpresspost from the Alberta origin, with an air segment on the lane in the same way as the Ontario routes. The eastern time-zone offset moves the dispatch cut-off earlier in local terms, so a Montreal order placed late in the afternoon will usually ship the following business day.</p><p class=\"text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Quebec carries the densest concentration of pharmaceutical and biotechnology activity in the country after Ontario, and the buyer expectations that come with it are documentation expectations. That suits how this catalogue is built: verification is per lot rather than per product, every lot is independently assayed before release, and both figures are published, purity and measured mass against the labelled content. The second one is the figure almost nobody in this market publishes, and it is the one that establishes whether a vial holds what its label claims.</p><p class=\"text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">The alternative this displaces in Quebec is usually an order routed in from a US or European site, and the difference is structural rather than a matter of preference. An inbound international parcel is subject to customs entry and CBSA examination, and research compounds are a category where examination and seizure genuinely occur. A parcel moving inside Canada has no import step at which any of that can happen, no brokerage charge and no possibility of a shipment being detained at a border.</p><p class=\"text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Documentation is published in English. That is a real limitation and worth naming rather than glossing: written support can be handled in French, but the laboratory certificates themselves are issued in English. What travels across the language boundary intact is the part that matters analytically, since a lot code, a measured purity and a measured mass verify identically regardless of the language the surrounding page is written in.</p><p class=\"text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Ordering is online only, with no Montreal location and no local collection. Parcels ship tracked and discreetly packaged, with no product names on the outer box.</p></div><section class=\"mt-9\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Delivery across <!-- -->Montreal</h2><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Montreal<!-- --> addresses in the<!-- --> <span class=\"font-mono\">H1, H2, H3, H7, J4</span> forward sortation areas are served on the <!-- -->2 business days<!-- --> Xpresspost expectation from the Alberta origin. Orders paid before the daily dispatch cut-off go out the same business day; after it, the next one.</p><ul class=\"mt-3 space-y-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5\"><li>The H prefixes cover the island of Montreal itself and run to the standard two-business-day Xpresspost expectation from Canadian stock.</li><li>H7 reaches Laval to the north; J4 covers Longueuil and the South Shore. Transit is normally identical, occasionally a day longer on the outer edges of the Montérégie.</li><li>Quebec City and the wider province generally run to the same two-day expectation, with rural routes on Canada Post's rural schedule rather than the urban Xpresspost standard.</li></ul><p class=\"mt-3 text-[13px]\"><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/shipping\">Full shipping and returns terms →</a></p></section><section class=\"mt-9\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">How these compounds are regulated in <!-- -->Quebec</h2><div class=\"mt-3 space-y-3\"><p class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Regulation of these compounds is federal, not provincial, so nothing about buying here differs between Quebec and any other province. Everything in this catalogue is supplied strictly as laboratory research material and holds no Health Canada authorisation as a health product: no DIN, no NPN, and no approval for any diagnostic or therapeutic purpose.</p><p class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Quebec imposes no separate provincial licence, permit or professional designation on the purchase of research-use-only material of this kind, and none is checked at checkout. The obligation that attaches is the one accepted at purchase: lawful laboratory research use under the applicable federal regulation.</p><p class=\"text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">It is worth naming the alternative this replaces, because it is the common one in Quebec: an offshore parcel from a US or European seller faces customs entry and CBSA examination on arrival, and the seller is generally under no obligation when a shipment is held or destroyed. A domestic order has no import step at which that can occur.</p></div><p class=\"mt-3 text-[13px]\"><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/are-peptides-legal-in-canada\">Are peptides legal in Canada? — the long answer →</a></p></section><section class=\"mt-9\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Ordering research peptides in <!-- -->Montreal<!-- --> — common questions</h2><dl class=\"mt-5 space-y-6\"><div><dt class=\"faq-question text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">How long does delivery to Montreal take?</dt><dd class=\"faq-answer mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">About two business days on Canada Post Xpresspost from the Alberta origin, tracked from dispatch. Quebec City typically runs to the same expectation.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"faq-question text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Is support available in French?</dt><dd class=\"faq-answer mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Written support can be handled in French. The laboratory certificates themselves are issued in English, though the analytical content travels across the language boundary intact: a lot code, a measured purity and a measured mass verify identically in either language.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"faq-question text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Why order domestically rather than from a US or European site?</dt><dd class=\"faq-answer mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Because a parcel moving inside Canada has no import step to fail. An offshore shipment is subject to customs entry and CBSA examination on arrival, research compounds are a category where seizure genuinely happens, and the foreign seller is generally under no obligation when it does.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"faq-question text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">Do you deliver to Laval and the South Shore?</dt><dd class=\"faq-answer mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Yes, on the same schedule as the island itself. Laval sits in the H7 prefix and Longueuil and the South Shore in J4, with occasional extra transit on the outer Montérégie routes.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"faq-question text-[15px] font-medium text-foreground\">How do I confirm the vial I received is the one that was tested?</dt><dd class=\"faq-answer mt-2 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Match the lot code printed on the vial label against the published certificate. Certificates are issued per lot rather than per product, and the batch lookup resolves a code straight to that lot's measured purity and measured content.</dd></div></dl></section><div class=\"mt-9 glass rounded-card border border-brand-300/30 dark:border-brand-500/20 p-6\"><h2 class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-foreground\">Verify before you buy</h2><p class=\"mt-3 text-[14px] text-foreground-secondary leading-relaxed\">Purity and measured content are both published for every lot, before anything is added to a cart. If you are already holding a vial, enter its lot code to pull up that batch’s report.</p><div class=\"mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-[13px]\"><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/verify\">Verify a batch code →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/certificates-of-analysis\">Browse all certificates →</a><a class=\"text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline\" href=\"/peptide-research/purity-vs-fill-accuracy\">Purity vs fill accuracy →</a></div></div><nav aria-label=\"Browse categories\" class=\"mt-9\"><h2 class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Browse the catalogue</h2><ul class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-[13px]\"><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/peptide-vials\">Peptides</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/intranasal-sprays\">Intranasal Sprays</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/capsules\">Capsules</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/bioregulators\">Bioregulators</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/aminos\">Aminos</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/collections/cosmetics\">Cosmetics</a></li></ul></nav><nav aria-label=\"Other cities\" class=\"mt-7\"><h2 class=\"font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-foreground-muted\">Other cities we ship to</h2><ul class=\"mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2 text-[13px]\"><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/edmonton\">Edmonton</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/calgary\">Calgary</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/vancouver\">Vancouver</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/winnipeg\">Winnipeg</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/toronto\">Toronto</a></li><li><a class=\"text-foreground-secondary hover:text-brand-600 dark:hover:text-brand-400\" href=\"/research-peptides/ottawa\">Ottawa</a></li></ul></nav><p class=\"mt-10 text-[12px] text-foreground-muted leading-relaxed\">Research use only. Materials supplied by Eppix Labs are intended strictly for in-vitro laboratory research. Not for human or veterinary use, and not for the diagnosis, treatment, cure or prevention of any condition. No dosing or administration guidance is provided.</p></div></section></div><!--$--><!--/$--></main><div class=\"no-overflow-x\"><footer class=\"glass\"><div class=\"border-b border-white/30 dark:border-border\"><ul class=\"mx-auto grid max-w-7xl gri